+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_01CkYBUz42NQPJWfnsCkZ3hp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012r9gaRndqeQgNmVfbCBNX5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# Contract: Constraint-Based Event Scheduler\n\n## API surface\n- [ ] `src/index.ts` exports `schedule(events, rooms, options)` as a named export → test: `import { schedule } from '../src/index'` works and returns `{ assignments, unscheduled }`.\n- [ ] Also export types `Event`, `Room`, `ScheduleOptions`, `Assignment`, `ScheduleResult` for consumers.\n\n## Core placement rules\n- [ ] Basic scheduling: a single event with no constraints gets scheduled in some room within the window → test: 1 event, 1 room, assignment present, unscheduled empty.\n- [ ] Room capacity: event.attendees must be <= room.capacity for the assigned room → test: event with attendees=10 and only a capacity=5 room available goes to `unscheduled`; if a capacity=10 room exists among several, it is chosen over smaller ones only as needed.\n- [ ] Default attendees is 1 when omitted → test: event without `attendees` fits in a capacity=1 room.\n- [ ] Time window: assignment.startTime >= options.startTime and assignment.endTime <= options.endTime → test: event whose duration doesn't fit anywhere in the window is unscheduled; event that fits is scheduled within bounds.\n- [ ] endTime = startTime + duration for every assignment → test: verify arithmetic on returned assignments.\n- [ ] Event too long for the window (duration > endTime-startTime) is unscheduled, not thrown → test.\n\n## Room gaps\n- [ ] Default gap is 15 minutes when `options.gap` is omitted → test: two events of duration 60 in a single room, window 180 min: only fit if second start >= first end + 15.\n- [ ] Custom gap respected → test: gap=0 allows back-to-back events (start2 == end1); gap=30 forces more separation, potentially causing one event to move rooms or become unscheduled given constrained rooms.\n- [ ] Events in *different* rooms do not need to respect the gap relative to each other → test: two overlapping-time events with attendees fitting, 2 rooms available, both scheduled concurrently in different rooms.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- [ ] Event B with prerequisite A: A's assignment.endTime + gap <= B's assignment.startTime → test: chain of 2 events A->B, verify ordering & gap in output.\n- [ ] Multiple prerequisites: B must start after ALL prerequisites end (+gap) → test: B depends on A1, A2; B.startTime >= max(A1.end, A2.end) + gap.\n- [ ] Prerequisite unscheduled => dependent cannot be scheduled → test: if A cannot fit (e.g. too long), B (which depends on A) ends up in `unscheduled` too, not incorrectly scheduled without its prerequisite.\n- [ ] Prerequisites can be scheduled in different rooms from dependents → test: no same-room requirement implied by prerequisite alone.\n\n## Cycle detection\n- [ ] Self-reference (`A` lists `A` as prerequisite) throws an Error synchronously when `schedule()` is called → test: `expect(() => schedule(...)).toThrow()`.\n- [ ] Two-node cycle (A->B, B->A) throws → test.\n- [ ] Longer cycle (A->B->C->A) throws → test.\n- [ ] Non-cyclic diamond dependency (A->B, A->C, B->D, C->D) does NOT throw and schedules correctly → test.\n- [ ] Reference to a nonexistent prerequisite id does not throw a cycle error (treated as unsatisfiable dependency, event becomes unscheduled) → test.\n\n## Preferred room\n- [ ] When preferredRoom is free/valid (capacity ok, no time conflict), event is placed there → test.\n- [ ] When preferredRoom lacks capacity, event is placed in another valid room instead (not left unscheduled if alternatives exist) → test.\n- [ ] When preferredRoom is unknown/nonexistent id, falls back to normal room selection → test.\n\n## Batch optimization\n- [ ] Greedy same-order placement would fail to schedule optimally in a constructed scenario; the scheduler finds the better packing → test: construct case where scheduling a big low-value event first blocks two smaller events from a single room/window, and assert the scheduler prefers packing more events (count of assignments maximized) over naive input-order greedy.\n- [ ] All unschedulable events appear in `unscheduled`, and `assignments.length + unscheduled.length === events.length` → test across multiple scenarios.\n- [ ] No double-booking: no two assignments in the same room have overlapping time ranges within `gap` of each other → test: for every scenario, verify pairwise room-time non-overlap with gap on the assignments returned.\n\n## Verification commands\n- `npm test` — vitest run, all tests pass\n- `npm run build` — tsc compiles with no errors\n- `npm run lint` — eslint passes with no errors\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":328,"cache_read_input_tokens":36525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":328},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519d7f72-c2bc-4155-923e-5133090440df","uuid":"aefbc5c1-a170-4610-ab88-6048d3eca539","request_id":"req_011CcaVYt2Hy22sGWDp76EfR"}
