+# Contract: Constraint-Based Event Scheduler
+
+## API surface
+- [x] `src/index.ts` exports `schedule(events, rooms, options)` as a named export → test: `import { schedule } from '../src/index'` works and returns `{ assignments, unscheduled }`.
+- [x] Also export types `Event`, `Room`, `ScheduleOptions`, `Assignment`, `ScheduleResult` for consumers.
+
+## Core placement rules
+- [x] Basic scheduling: a single event with no constraints gets scheduled in some room within the window → test: 1 event, 1 room, assignment present, unscheduled empty.
+- [x] Room capacity: event.attendees must be <= room.capacity for the assigned room → test: event with attendees=10 and only a capacity=5 room available goes to `unscheduled`; if a capacity=10 room exists among several, it is chosen over smaller ones only as needed.
+- [x] Default attendees is 1 when omitted → test: event without `attendees` fits in a capacity=1 room.
+- [x] Time window: assignment.startTime >= options.startTime and assignment.endTime <= options.endTime → test: event whose duration doesn't fit anywhere in the window is unscheduled; event that fits is scheduled within bounds.
+- [x] endTime = startTime + duration for every assignment → test: verify arithmetic on returned assignments.
+- [x] Event too long for the window (duration > endTime-startTime) is unscheduled, not thrown → test.
+
+## Room gaps
+- [x] Default gap is 15 minutes when `options.gap` is omitted → test: two events of duration 60 in a single room, window 180 min: only fit if second start >= first end + 15.
+- [x] Custom gap respected → test: gap=0 allows back-to-back events (start2 == end1); gap=30 forces more separation, potentially causing one event to move rooms or become unscheduled given constrained rooms.
+- [x] Events in *different* rooms do not need to respect the gap relative to each other → test: two overlapping-time events with attendees fitting, 2 rooms available, both scheduled concurrently in different rooms.
+
+## Prerequisites
+- [x] Event B with prerequisite A: A's assignment.endTime + gap <= B's assignment.startTime → test: chain of 2 events A->B, verify ordering & gap in output.
+- [x] Multiple prerequisites: B must start after ALL prerequisites end (+gap) → test: B depends on A1, A2; B.startTime >= max(A1.end, A2.end) + gap.
+- [x] Prerequisite unscheduled => dependent cannot be scheduled → test: if A cannot fit (e.g. too long), B (which depends on A) ends up in `unscheduled` too, not incorrectly scheduled without its prerequisite.
+- [x] Prerequisites can be scheduled in different rooms from dependents → test: no same-room requirement implied by prerequisite alone.
+
+## Cycle detection
+- [x] Self-reference (`A` lists `A` as prerequisite) throws an Error synchronously when `schedule()` is called → test: `expect(() => schedule(...)).toThrow()`.
+- [x] Two-node cycle (A->B, B->A) throws → test.
+- [x] Longer cycle (A->B->C->A) throws → test.
+- [x] Non-cyclic diamond dependency (A->B, A->C, B->D, C->D) does NOT throw and schedules correctly → test.
+- [x] Reference to a nonexistent prerequisite id does not throw a cycle error (treated as unsatisfiable dependency, event becomes unscheduled) → test.
+
+## Preferred room
+- [x] When preferredRoom is free/valid (capacity ok, no time conflict), event is placed there → test.
+- [x] When preferredRoom lacks capacity, event is placed in another valid room instead (not left unscheduled if alternatives exist) → test.
+- [x] When preferredRoom is unknown/nonexistent id, falls back to normal room selection → test.
+
+## Batch optimization
+- [x] Greedy same-order placement would fail to schedule optimally in a constructed scenario; the scheduler finds the better packing → test: construct case where scheduling a big low-value event first blocks two smaller events from a single room/window, and assert the scheduler prefers packing more events (count of assignments maximized) over naive input-order greedy.
+- [x] All unschedulable events appear in `unscheduled`, and `assignments.length + unscheduled.length === events.length` → test across multiple scenarios.
+- [x] No double-booking: no two assignments in the same room have overlapping time ranges within `gap` of each other → test: for every scenario, verify pairwise room-time non-overlap with gap on the assignments returned.
+
+## Verification commands
+- `npm test` — vitest run, all tests pass
+- `npm run build` — tsc compiles with no errors
+- `npm run lint` — eslint passes with no errors
